  "worked_solution": "First, we must determine the average temperature in Oslo during the month of January. Since we know that the temperature decreases on average by ${6.2}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}$ compared to November, we subtract the variation in temperature from the average temperature in November. This gives\n\n$$\n{3.3}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}-{6.2}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}=-{2.9}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.\n$$\n\nNow, we must determine the temperature during the month of March. Since we know that the temperature increases on average by ${4.6}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}$ compared to January, we add the variation in temperature to the average temperature in January. This gives\n\n$$\n-{2.9}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}+{4.6}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}={1.7}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the average temperature in Oslo in March is ${1.7}^{∘}\\,\\text{C}.$",
